From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patch Maintainers <patches@example.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +01:00
Subject: [PATCH] fix: keep initial workload minimums valid during scaling

Initial pending elastic workloads can retain stale minimum counts when the job changes size. A previously admitted workload can also become invalid if it shrinks below its minimum while awaiting readmission.

Synchronize first-admission minimums with the job and cap readmission minimums at the current count. Upstream handles admitted and replacement scale-down.
---
